@title Why a sidewalk-repair permit takes 29 days
@subtitle How an application moves through the office, last quarter, 1,846 applications
@date Last quarter
@width wide

# The three-minute version

kpi Median time, received to issued | 29 days | service charter target: 15 working days | bad

The median sidewalk-repair permit took 29 days from received to issued last quarter. The charter promises 15 working days, so fewer than half of permits meet it. The fastest 10% finish in 8 days and the slowest 10% take 71 days or more. Three places stand out: the wait for utility replies, applications bounced at the first check, and the heritage review.

kpi Applications | 1,846 | last quarter | neutral
kpi Fastest 10% | 8 days | finish within | good
kpi Slowest 10% | 71+ days | take at least | bad
kpi Bounced at first check | 31% | usually a missing site plan | bad
kpi Issued | 94% | 6% rejected or withdrawn | neutral

